      <div class="modal-body">
        <p class="p-modal text-justify">
            Since November 2018, New Caledonia’s only private hospital has been the Clinique Île Nou-Magnin, located in Nouville, Nouméa. It brought together the three former private clinics of Nouméa (Magnin, Baie des Citrons and Anse Vata) on a single site, with about 263 beds. Along with the CHT, it is one of the two providers of care that needs a specialized technical platform. Private practitioners (médecins libéraux) provide much of the outpatient primary and specialist care, especially in Greater Nouméa.
        </p>
        <p><strong>Authorization and Classification</strong></p>
        <p class="p-modal text-justify">
            Private facilities are regulated under the same authorization system as public ones. Under Deliberation 429, Article 2, the carte sanitaire is the basis for authorizing installations, heavy equipment and regulated care activities “pour le secteur public ou privé” (for the public or private sector). An authorization lapses if the program is not carried out within four years for the public sector, or two years for the private sector. Authorizations cannot be transferred, and they may be suspended or withdrawn for breaches of public health rules. The health section of the Comité territorial de l’organisation sanitaire et sociale is consulted on any creation, extension or conversion of a public or private health establishment (Article 11).
        </p>
        <p class="p-modal text-justify">
            <strong>Note:</strong> Unlike the other countries in this series, New Caledonia’s authorization system covers private facilities by law. A private facility’s level of care within each scheme (for example, its perinatal or emergency level) is meant to be fixed by government arrêté under Deliberation 171, Article 17. Record the Clinique Île Nou-Magnin as “Private hospital — authorized under Délibération n° 429,” and confirm any scheme-specific level against the relevant arrêté rather than the clinic’s own description.
        </p>
        <ul data-info-section="role">
            <li>Provide private medical, surgical and obstetric hospital care with a specialized technical platform, complementing the CHT</li>
            <li>Participate in the authorized care networks (for example, perinatal care) under agreements with public facilities</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="p-modal text-justify">
            <em><strong>Note:</strong> This section is aligned with Délibération n° 429 of 3 November 1993, Articles 2 and 11, and Délibération n° 171 of 25 January 2001, Article 17. Facility details come from secondary sources and the Vice-rectorat de la Nouvelle-Calédonie.</em>
        </p>
